From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:52:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS-Mythic: #79 TCP state numbering, NSI bypass, minidump
 gate, alert-probe TEB guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#79 SOLVED+VERIFIED (ml479): Steam's WebUITransport authenticates its loopback
peer via GetExtendedTcpTable(AF_INET, OWNER_PID_CONNECTIONS) — matching
row.localport == peer.remoteport, requiring state == ESTAB, then comparing
dwOwningPid. Every connection was rejected because config_ios.h undefines
HAVE_NETINET_TCP_FSM_H (the iOS SDK ships no netinet/tcp_fsm.h), so sock.c fell
back to LINUX-numbered TCPS_* while Darwin's TCP_CONNECTION_INFO reports BSD
numbering: LISTEN(1) matched TCPS_ESTABLISHED(1) and ESTABLISHED(4) matched
TCPS_FIN_WAIT_1(4). The ESTAB table therefore held exactly the three listeners
and none of the real connections.

server/sock.c: BSD-numbered TCPS_* under __APPLE__ (Linux block kept in #else).
Verified — listeners now report LISTEN, real pairs report ESTAB with both pids,
and "Connection rejected" went 11/11 -> 0.

Also in this stack:
- dlls/nsi/nsi.c: NsiEnumerateObjectsAllParametersEx falls back to a unix call
  when \\.\Nsi won't open (nsiproxy.sys is absent on iOS and its service is
  disabled), so the TCP tables can be served in-process.
- dlls/dbghelp/minidump.c: header-only MiniDumpWriteDump — Valve's dump-buffer
  ratchet was the #79-era death cause.
- dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c (ml482): NtAlertThreadByThreadId needs no TEB, but its
  two iOS diagnostics read NtCurrentTeb()->ClientId.UniqueThread (TEB+0x48).
  Threads created directly by CEF/FEX have no TEB, so the PROBE null-dereffed
  and killed the app the moment the login-window popup brought new threads onto
  that path. Read the tid defensively.
- dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c: #81 finding preserved in comments; the xlate
  wraps are reverted (they are needed only with jitless off, and they crashed
  the shipping config).
- socket.c / system.c / sync.c: supporting iOS fixes.

(cherry picked from commit 73fc9ef2e261ccdbfc55886509320f8523d46e4e)
Madeira-commit: d3d5a179a53b2968de243a6ff4a381d87a892dfa
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
